---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import HorizontalCard from "../components/HorizontalCard.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Projects" sideBarActiveItemID="projects">
  <div>
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold mb-5">Featured Projects</div>
  </div>

  <HorizontalCard
    title="Pothole Avoidance and Motion Planning with Deep Reinforcement Learning"
    img="/projects/pothole-avoidance.webp"
    desc="Dec 2025 - Jun 2026. Role: dataset collection, object detection, path planning design. An autonomous vehicle that spots road damage in real time and chooses a path that avoids it without jolting passengers. I gathered 16,000 annotated images of Indonesian roads, then combined a YOLOv11 detector with a DQN agent inside CARLA. A reward function balances pothole avoidance against ride comfort. When training first failed to converge, I traced the problem to the reward weighting and to inconsistent detections between training and evaluation. Fixing both gave a 100% avoidance rate in bright weather, 84% in rain, and a longitudinal acceleration of 0.36 m/s². Presented at ASCC 2026. Tech: YOLOv11, DQN, Python, TensorFlow, PyTorch, OpenCV, CARLA."
    url="https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1-jvc4ygdh-QeUgsxYcUha1QzKD3QeQf6?usp=drive_link"
    badge="ASCC 2026"
  />
  <div class="divider my-0"></div>
  <HorizontalCard
    title="ASRS RTOS with Robotic Arm"
    img="/projects/asrs-rtos.webp"
    desc="Designed the system architecture for an automated sorting and storage system. Integrated a conveyor belt with ultrasonic sensors, an RFID reader, and a robotic arm to sort items into a dynamic storage rack based on RFID attributes. Included an OLED display for real-time monitoring and an alert system triggered by specific temperature (> 26°C) and humidity (> 65%) thresholds."
    url="https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1GI7tA-V4892xV1vhsZZr-NjpnZp3gNBA?usp=drive_link"
  />
  <div class="divider my-0"></div>
  <HorizontalCard
    title="Industrial Communication & Integration: Mitsubishi PLC"
    img="/projects/plc-mitsubishi-integration.png"
    desc="Developed a bidirectional industrial communication architecture integrating a Programmable Logic Controller (PLC) with supervisory systems. Utilized KEPServerEX as an intermediary to seamlessly connect the PLC with a SCADA system and a PostgreSQL database for data monitoring and logging."
    url="https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1J7sXWeYK4Ty-lu6aB4aFfoX5FeN828sq?hl=id"
  />
  <div class="divider my-0"></div>
  <HorizontalCard
    title="High-Speed Digital Signal Integrity Analysis"
    img="/projects/signal-integrity.png"
    desc="Conducted extensive signal integrity and crosstalk analysis for high-speed circuit designs. Utilized LTspice, Serial Link Designer, and SIMBEOR to evaluate transmission line reflections, PCB trace crosstalk, and microstrip discontinuities. Assessed backplane performance using statistical eye diagrams and optimized Continuous-Time Linear Equalizer (CTLE) and Decision Feedback Equalizer (DFE) parameters."
    url="https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1r6tFX8c_bt-huGceYxt2Oa2AsaRLqohH?hl=id"
  />
  <div class="divider my-0"></div>
  <HorizontalCard
    title="IIoT-Based 3-Axis Automated Storage and Retrieval System (ASRS)"
    img="/projects/asrs.webp"
    desc="Oct 2025 - Jan 2026. Role: System Engineer. A fully automated pick-and-place storage system that can be supervised remotely. I wrote the ladder logic for the three-axis motion sequence, giving fully repeatable cycles of 10 seconds at most, and designed an HMI with live visualization, diagnostics, and manual override. A secure IIoT layer with MQTT and Node-RED sends data to a cloud dashboard and logs history to PostgreSQL, with control signals kept separate from monitoring data to keep communication stable. Tech: Omron PLC (ladder diagram), Weintek HMI, MQTT, Node-RED, PostgreSQL."
    url="https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1jE8wLgeluKBA7dq635SnGhEWXc8qoOpI?usp=drive_link"
  />
  <div class="divider my-0"></div>
  <HorizontalCard
    title="Automated Fish Pond Monitoring with Smartphone Integration"
    img="/projects/fish-pond.webp"
    desc="Jun 2024 - Aug 2024. Role: Embedded Engineer. A real-time monitoring system covering water level, weather, and air flow across three ponds. I designed the sensor network and ESP32 firmware and built an Android app that shows live readings, with a focus on low-latency, dependable delivery so operators can react to abnormal conditions early. Tech: C++, C#, ESP32, IoT sensors, Android Studio."
    url="https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1LYigdswihRhi_6kHhhzPZSRFnlrN2-oI?usp=drive_link"
  />

  <div>
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold mb-5 mt-10">Other Work</div>
  </div>

  <HorizontalCard
    title="SMD Pick and Place Machine Operation"
    img="/projects/smd-pick-and-place.png"
    desc="Operated Surface-Mount Device (SMD) pick and place machinery for printed circuit board (PCB) assembly. Managed component loading, feeder setup, and precision placement to ensure highly accurate, automated surface mount technology (SMT) manufacturing and hardware production."
    url="https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1o4jWAFa6ATF3D7tVbmOZaV-P5WURToxb?hl=id"
  />
  <div class="divider my-0"></div>
  <HorizontalCard
    title="MOZA R12 Steering System Replica"
    img="/projects/moza-replica.webp"
    desc="Jul 2025 - Aug 2025, PT. AVS Simulator. Built a replica of a MOZA R12 steering system on an STM32 microcontroller for a truck driving simulator."
    url="#"
  />
  <div class="divider my-0"></div>
  <HorizontalCard
    title="Humanoid Robots"
    img="/projects/humanoid.webp"
    desc="Co-led a five-person mechanical team that developed two humanoid robots from start to finish. The team assembled its own Anet A8 3D printer from parts to save budget, then used it to enlarge the robots' chest structure for a bigger controller compartment and to print replacements whenever parts broke."
    url="https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1-jvc4ygdh-QeUgsxYcUha1QzKD3QeQf6?usp=drive_link"
  />
  <div class="divider my-0"></div>
  <HorizontalCard
    title="Bridge Monitoring System"
    img="/projects/bridge-monitoring.webp"
    desc="Led a three-person team in delivering a bridge monitoring system, taking it from client requirements through to a working prototype."
    url="https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1d8NjXTs6BW-vLpcFc-MIpx3VtTO8jtxP?usp=drive_link"
  />
</BaseLayout>